NAME
====

**jeep-dep** - add, edit or remove dependency information in a Janet bundle

SYNOPSIS
========

**jeep-dep** [**-v** | **--vendor**] **add** [**-a** | **--autotag**] _deps_ ...

**jeep-dep** [**-v** | **--vendor**] **edit** [**-a** | **--autotag**] _dep_
             [_key_ _value_] ...

**jeep-dep** [**-v** | **--vendor**] **rem** _deps_ ...

**jeep-dep** [**-v** | **--vendor**] **tidy**

DESCRIPTION
===========

**jeep-dep** adds, edits or removes dependency information in a bundle's __info
file__. This command does not install dependencies; that is the responsibility
of `jeep-prep(1)`.

Each operation is a subcommand. The **--vendor** option applies to whichever
subcommand is used and so is given before the subcommand's name.

Options
-------

- **-v**, **--vendor**:
  Operates on the dependencies that will be vendored rather than the
  dependencies that will be installed to the __syspath__. Vendoring is discussed
  below in `<Vendoring>`.

Subcommands
-----------

- **add** [**-a** | **--autotag**] _deps_ ...:
  Adds one or more dependencies to the bundle's __info file__. Each dependency
  can be specified by a URL or a JDN struct/table. A struct/table must contain
  the ``:name`` and ``:url`` keys. A dependency that cannot be resolved to a URL
  is an error. A dependency that is already listed is skipped.

- **edit** [**-a** | **--autotag**] _dep_ [_key_ _value_] ...:
  Edits a single dependency in the bundle's __info file__. The dependency can be
  specified by its name or its URL and must already be listed.

  Each _key_ is a keyword and each _value_ is any JDN value. Each pair is set on
  the dependency: a _key_ that is already present has its _value_ replaced and a
  _key_ that is absent is added. Keys that are not named are left untouched and
  a _value_ of ``nil`` removes the _key_. If the dependency is listed as a bare
  name, it is converted into a struct.

- **rem** _deps_ ...:
  Removes one or more dependencies from the bundle's __info file__. Each
  dependency can be specified by its name or its URL.

- **tidy**:
  Sorts the bundle's dependencies by name. Comments and blank lines in the
  __info file__ are preserved.

The **--autotag** option, available on **add** and **edit**, sets the
``:tag`` key of each dependency to the SHA of the current commit of the
dependency's repository. The dependency must have a ``:url`` key for this to be
possible.

Vendoring
---------

A bundle's __info file__ can contain dependency information in an array/tuple
mapped to the ``:dependencies`` key. By default, dependencies that are added,
edited or removed using **jeep-dep** are added to, edited in or removed from
this data structure. Dependencies that are listed in this data structure are
installed into the __syspath__. This will either be the global syspath or
`./_system`, the local syspath, if the user is using the **--local** flag as
described in `jeep(1)`.

Janet does not support the installation of multiple versions of a dependency.
To avoid version conflicts, a user may prefer to vendor dependencies.
**jeep-dep** supports this with the **--vendor** option. Vendored dependencies
are listed in an array/tuple under the ``:vendored`` keyword.

A vendored dependency is similar to an ordinary dependency. That is, it is a
struct/table containing the ``:name`` and ``:url`` keys. It can also include the
``:tag``, ``:prefix``, and ``:paths`` keys. If the ``:paths`` key is present, a
vendored dependency will be fetched from the specified URL and the values used
to copy files into the bundle. If the values are strings, the relative path of
the source file matches the relative path of the destination file. However, if
the value is a two-element array/tuple, the file located at the path in the
first value will be copied to the path in the second value. See `<EXAMPLES>`
below.

For more information about the __info file__, the __bundle script__ and the
__syspath__, see CONCEPTS in `jeep(1)`.

EXAMPLES
========

To add a dependency to the __info file__:

````
$ jeep dep add https://example.org/foo.git
````

To edit a dependency in the __info file__ so it has the SHA of the current
commit:

````
$ jeep dep edit -a foo
````

To remove a dependency from the __info file__:

````
$ jeep dep rem foo
````

To sort the dependencies in the __info file__ by name:

````
$ jeep dep tidy
````

To add two dependencies that will be vendored:

````
$ jeep dep -v add https://example.org/foo.git https://example.org/bar.git
````

To add a vendored dependency that will selectively copy files:

````
$ jeep dep -v add '{:name "foo" \
                    :url "https://example.org/foo" \
                    :prefix "deps" \
                    :paths [["a.janet" "b.janet"] \
                            ["c.janet" "c/init.janet"]]}'
````

To set a key on a vendored dependency:

````
$ jeep dep -v edit foo :prefix '"deps/foo"'
````

To remove a key from a vendored dependency:

````
$ jeep dep -v edit foo :prefix nil
````

